
<opts>
<isrc>keybd</isrc>
<iname>INPUT</iname>
<iecho>yes</iecho>
<odest>screen</odest>
<oname>OUTPUT</oname>
<onewl>lf</onewl>
<scrfont>swiss11</scrfont>
<statwin>on</statwin>
<cfmt>~%month,%prin</cfmt>
<citer>60</citer>
<cdisp>fmtlist</cdisp>
<rtype>fmt</rtype>
<rfmt>\n\N   \V\n\T</rfmt>
<rall>yes</rall>
<starg>ugga</starg>
<srpl></srpl>
<scount>1</scount>
<sout>yes</sout>
<nfmt>fixed</nfmt>
<ndec>3</ndec>
<nang>degrees</nang>
<pltng>off</pltng>
<xmax>235.000</xmax>
<xmin>0.000</xmin>
<ymax>200000.000</ymax>
<ymin>0.000</ymin>
<xintrvls>10</xintrvls>
<yintrvls>10</yintrvls>
<xycells>month,prin</xycells>
<cell>
<cname>apr</cname>
<text>annual periodic interest rate</text>
<val>0.14</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>home</cname>
<text>Amortiation calculator.  Currently set up to simulate paying off a note at a set interest rate.  Minor changes will allow it to compute the future value of a sum given an interest rate and a payment amount.

DIRECTORY:
  month-- payment number
  prin -- principal amount
  apr -- set to annual periodic interest rate...
  itm -- interest paid this month... computed
  mi -- monthly interest rate... computed
  pymt -- monthly payment.... set to payment

SETUP:
    In execution preferences:
           set Execution Results to Formatted
           set number of iterations to a number larger than necessary to pay off note or accumulate sum.

USAGE:
     Set month to 0.  
     Fill in payment amount (pymt) if it hasn't been already.
     Fill in apr percentage (apr) if it hasn't been already.
     Fill in principal amount. (prin)
    
     Return to home cell, and select Execute from the Special menu.</text>
<val>244.000</val>
<script>prin()
month()</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>itm</cname>
<text>interest paid this month</text>
<val>2292.241</val>
<script>mi!*prin</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>mi</cname>
<text>monthly interest rate</text>
<val>0.012</val>
<script>apr/12</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>month</cname>
<val>0</val>
<script>month+1</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>prin</cname>
<text>Principal amount
</text>
<val>196270.030</val>
<script>if(prin>pymt) {
    prin+itm!-pymt
} elseif(prin>0) {
    0
} else {
    exit
}</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>pymt</cname>
<text>monthly payment
</text>
<val>2500</val></cell></eof>